  "body": "Part of #3663 (step U8 of the tool library refit). This PR changes the frame of the tool library window. It does not change the content of the pages; U9 to U12 change the pages.\n\n## What changed\n\n- New file `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_library_dialog/frame.rs` with one header and one footer for all pages.\n- The header has these parts:\n  - \"‹ List\" when the tool editor, the component editor or the read-only holder view is open.\n  - The title. A list page shows \"Tool library\". An editor shows the tool, holder or component name and a dim subtitle (for example \"end mill · T1\").\n  - The \"Cutting tools\" and \"Holders\" tabs.\n  - A \"×\" close button at the right. Its AccessKit name is \"Close the tool library\".\n- The footer shows a hint on the left. Its buttons are:\n  - list pages and the holder view: **Close**;\n  - tool editor: **Duplicate** (disabled, the hover text gives the reason, follow-up #4340), **Cancel** and **Apply**;\n  - component editor: **Cancel** and **Apply component**.\n- The header and the footer are `egui::Panel`s in the window. The footer stays at the bottom of the window while a list scrolls.\n- The window has no egui title bar and no shadow. The header replaces the title bar. The AccessKit name of the window stays \"Tool library\".\n- Apply queues the same commands as before (`ChangeTool` or `ReshapeTool`, then `SetToolNumber` when the number changed). Apply stays one undo step.\n- Cancel and \"‹ List\" drop the unapplied draft and go back to the list, as the old way back did. Close and \"×\" are view state and queue no command.\n- `holder_view.rs` and `component_edit.rs` lose their own back buttons and headings, because the header now has them. \"Apply component\" moves to the footer. Sync and Save stay in the page.\n- The tool editor loses its \"Tool: name\" heading and its Apply row.\n- Visual style follows the rules on #4245 with the existing theme tokens: flat, hairline panel separators, no shadow, Apply filled with the theme accent. There is no new theme or kit crate.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/4334-tool-library-dialog-frame.md`.\n  - The window stays non-modal, at the same place and size.\n  - There is no egui title bar.\n  - The tab keeps the label \"Cutting tools\": the ribbon already has a \"Tools\" button.\n  - Duplicate is disabled until #4340.\n  - The back button reads \"‹ List\", because the egui fonts have no \"←\".\n\nThe PR does not touch the stack group of #4331 (`stack.rs`, `assembly_group.rs`, `tool_tab.rs`).\n\n## Screenshots (1366 × 768, rendered headlessly)\n\nBefore (main) and after (this branch):\n\n| Page | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Tool list | ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4365/before/1-tool-list.png) | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4365/after/1-tool-list.png) |\n| Tool editor | ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4365/before/2-tool-editor.png) | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4365/after/2-tool-editor.png) |\n| Holder list | ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4365/before/3-holder-list.png) | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4365/after/3-holder-list.png) |\n| Holder view | ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4365/before/4-holder-view.png) | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4365/after/4-holder-view.png) |\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- New `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_library_frame.rs` (5 tests):\n  - `the_tool_list_has_the_header_and_the_close_footer`: the title, the tabs, the \"×\", no way back, the hint, Close enabled, and no Apply, Cancel or Duplicate. Close closes the window and queues no command.\n  - `the_tool_editor_has_the_back_button_and_the_apply_footer`: \"‹ List\", the name and the tabs. Apply and Cancel are enabled, Duplicate is disabled, and there is no footer Close.\n  - `cancel_drops_the_draft_and_apply_stays_one_undo_step`: Cancel queues nothing and keeps the tool. Apply adds one history entry, and one undo restores the tool.\n  - `back_leaves_each_editor_and_the_header_closes_the_window`: the way back works from the tool editor and from the holder view, and the \"×\" closes the window.\n  - `each_face_has_its_hint`: the hint of each page, and which pages show the way back.\n- `layout_window_tool_library` asserts the header row (title, tabs, \"×\") and the footer row (hint, then Close at the right).\n- `layout_window_tool_editor` asserts \"‹ List\" with the name beside it, and Duplicate, Cancel and Apply on one footer row.\n- Changed tests:\n  - `tool_properties::edit_in_tool_library_opens_the_window_on_the_tool` finds the tool name, not \"Tool: name\".\n  - `tool_shape_window::new_tool_matching_saved_name_has_no_empty_target_actions` clicks the Close of the Properties pane. The library window now has a Close button too.\n- The `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` goes up by 5. No test is deleted or ignored. No snapshot PNG changes.\n\n## Gate results (head b1365b233)\n\n| Step | Where | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (ui build, ui lib, 8 ui suites) | Mac, lane 1 | 10 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (7.4 min) |\n| `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` (full lib, before the last two test fixes) | winbuild | 1762 passed, 2 failed (the two changed tests above) |\n| the same filtered to `tool_library page_layout_tool_library tool_shape_window tool_properties setup_wcs` after the fixes | winbuild | 93 passed, 0 failed |\n| `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` | Mac | clean |\n| `cargo xtask gate light` | Mac | 6 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (17.3 min) |\n\n`setup_wcs_tests::the_combo_lists_the_setups_post_range_by_its_names` (#4322, red on main) passed in these runs.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The window was not used by hand in the desktop app. The screenshots come from the egui_kittest renderer.\n- A drag on the window background that moves the window (`WindowDrag::Anywhere`).\n- The component editor footer is covered by the existing component tests (`component_edit::APPLY`, `component_edit::BACK`). It has no new test of its own.\n\nChangelog: The tool library window has one header (the way back, the name, the Cutting tools and Holders tabs) and one footer on each page (a hint; Close, or Duplicate, Cancel and Apply).\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #4334\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
